  "actions": [
    {
      "operation": "Extend/prolong an existing protruding lever",
      "parameters": {
        "extension_length": "5cm",
        "extension_direction_definition": "Along the lever's existing protrusion axis, defined by the outward normal of the lever top end-cap face"
      },
      "target": "black lever",
      "relational_constraint": "Increase the lever length in the forward ('to the front') direction, i.e., further out from the main body in the same direction it is currently sticking out. Based on multiview images and section definitions, the only clearly defined black lever is the actuation lever/rod (S7); therefore, interpret 'front/protruding' as the lever's outward protrusion direction (along its axis) to improve reach/manipulation without changing lever alignment or mating at its base.",
      "unresolved_reference": "User wording says 'to the front' but the multiview images show the black lever as a primarily vertical actuation rod above the brew head. If 'front' was intended to mean horizontal (toward the cavity opening), the target would instead be a separate portafilter/handle-like component that is not explicitly defined as a section in model.json. Proceeding with the best-defined 'black lever' section (S7) and extending along its current axis (top end-cap normal).",
      "target section code": [
        "S7"
      ],
      "target face code": [
        "0039",
        "0038"
      ],
